  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge in Practice: sharing agroecological knowledge throughout Latin America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Smallholder farmers in Latin America can benefit from adopting an approach to food production that considers the environmental, social, and economic impacts on communities and contributes to food security. At the IAF, we support community-led solutions to expand economic opportunity in Brazil. Our grantee partner, Centro de Estudos e Promoo da Agricultura de Grupo (CEPAGRO), works with grantee partners throughout Latin America to develop a collaborative network of farmers and a learning platform to share training opportunities and best practices in sustainable agriculture. CEPAGRO is also supporting the organic production and waste management activities of two local organizations in Santa Catarina, Brazil, organizations that IAF grantee partners from across the region can visit for on-the-ground experience and peer-to-peer learning.</narrative>
  </description>
